🧾 Recommended AI Certifications (2025–2026)

Here are realistic, recognized certifications that complement your analytics profile:

1. Microsoft Certified: Azure AI Fundamentals (AI-900)

Time commitment: 20–30 hours total

Focus: Core concepts of AI and ML, computer vision, NLP, responsible AI.

Why it fits: Low barrier, integrates with Power BI and Azure services; aligns with Microsoft ecosystem you already use.

Next step: Later consider Azure AI Engineer Associate (AI-102) for applied LLM and chatbot work.

2. Google Cloud AI or ML Certifications

Option A: Google Cloud AI Fundamentals (Course on Coursera)

Option B: Google Cloud Machine Learning Engineer Professional (advanced)

Good for cloud exposure and MLOps understanding.

3. IBM Applied AI Professional Certificate (Coursera)

Focus: AI applications, NLP, computer vision, and Python-based AI tools.

Benefit: Practical, portfolio-oriented with notebooks you can upload to GitHub.

Difficulty: Medium; takes 2–3 months part-time.

4. AWS Certified Machine Learning Engineer – Associate (launching 2025)

Focus: Data preprocessing, model training, deployment on AWS SageMaker.

For later: Once you’re comfortable with cloud data workflows.

5. OpenAI / DeepLearning.AI: “ChatGPT for Data Analysts” (Coursera / short course)

Practical, short (10–12 hours)

Focuses on using generative AI to clean, summarize, and visualize data — directly applicable to BI and Power BI workflows.
